prompt.text:
Implement an in-memory lab-submission module.

Export the following API:

```ts
export interface LabSubmissionInput {
  readonly ownerId: string;
  readonly assignmentId: string;
  readonly summary: string;
  readonly attachment: string;
}
export interface LabSubmission extends LabSubmissionInput {
  readonly id: string;
}
export const EMPTY_LAB_SUBMISSION: LabSubmission;
export const LAB_SUBMISSION_LABELS: { readonly one: string; readonly many: string };
export class LabSubmissionStore {
  constructor(initial?: readonly LabSubmission[]);
  findById(id: string): Promise<LabSubmission | undefined>;
  update(submission: LabSubmission): Promise<boolean>;
}
```

`EMPTY_LAB_SUBMISSION` has all five strings empty. Labels are `"lab submission"` and `"lab submissions"`. Constructor records with duplicate IDs use the last occurrence. `findById` returns an independent copy or `undefined`; an empty ID is simply not found.

`update` returns false when the ID is absent. When present, it updates only `summary` and `attachment`; the stored `id`, `ownerId`, and `assignmentId` must remain unchanged. Empty strings are valid field values. Returned and input objects must never be mutated or retained by reference. Preserve no ordering-dependent public behavior.

